{"_id":"696631c43eeddc26d7c3a612","roadmapSlug":"ruby","nodeId":"WMa8k6sbhow-TXNibFj0a","description":"# Nil\n\n`nil` represents the absence of a value or a non-existent object. It's a special object in Ruby that signifies emptiness or the lack of a meaningful result. Think of it as a placeholder indicating that a variable or expression doesn't currently hold a valid value.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"Nothingness and the truth","url":"http://ruby-for-beginners.rubymonstas.org/conditionals/nothing_and_truth.html","_id":"6a7f4b2bcb44947debcfd7e1"},{"type":"article","title":"Everything You Need to Know About Nil","url":"https://www.rubyguides.com/2018/01/ruby-nil/","_id":"6a7f4b2bcb44947debcfd7e2"},{"type":"article","title":"True, False, and Nil","url":"https://ruby-for-beginners.rubymonstas.org/built_in_classes/true_false_nil.html","_id":"6a7f4b2bcb44947debcfd7e3"},{"type":"video","title":"Ruby Nil Explained","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mBJrQ84f6-4","_id":"6a7f4b2bcb44947debcfd7e4"}],"createdAt":"2026-01-13T11:51:32.690Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:06:51.273Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/ruby/content/WMa8k6sbhow-TXNibFj0a.md"}